## Product Detection Service

Product detection service is used for detecting products in the image.

**Methods:**

### Detect

*[Example](examples/product/detect_product_from_image.py)*

```python
product_detection.detect(image_path)
```

Finds all products on the image.

| Argument          | Type    | Required | Notes                                                                                                                                          |
| ----------------- | ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| image_path        | image   | required | image where to detect products. Image can pass from url, local path or bytes.                             |


Response:

```json
{
    'status': '1',
    'locates':
    [
        {'label': 'product', 'score': 0.959, 'bbox': [193, 160, 379, 363]},
        "...",
        {'label': 'product', 'score': 0.563, 'bbox': [233, 754, 323, 772]}
    ]
}}
```

| Element                        | Type    | Description                                                  |
| ------------------------------ | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| status   | string | status of the delete operation .  |
| bbox                            | array  | list of parameters of the bounding box for this product (on processedImage) |
| label                    | string   | Label detection     |


## Product Verify Service

*[Example](examples/product/verify_product_from_image.py)*

Product verification service is used for comparing two images.
A source image should contain only one product which will be compared to all products on the target image.

**Methods:**

### Verify

```python
product_verify: ProductVerifyService = deep_vision.init_product_verify_service(
    VERIFICATION_API_KEY)
    
product_verify.verify(source_image_path, target_image_path)
```

Compares two images provided in arguments. Source image should contain only one product, it will be compared to all products in the target image.

| Argument            | Type    | Required | Notes                                                                                                                                                 |
| ------------------  | ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| source_image_path   | image   | required | file to be verified. Image can pass from url, local path or bytes.                                            |
| target_image_path   | image   | required | reference file to check the source file. Image can pass from url, local path or bytes.                       |

Response:

```json
{
    'status': 'completed',
    'result': {
        'source_image_product':
        {
            'embedding': [-0.03902999835598629, '...', -0.028654199455642616],
            'bbox': [0, 0, 624, 773]
        },
            'product_matches':
            {
                'embedding': [-0.03902999835598629, '...', 5, -0.028654199455642616],
                'bbox': [0, 0, 624, 773],
                'verify': 'True',
                'similarity': array([[0.]])
        }
    }
}
```

| Element                        | Type    | Description                                                  |
| ------------------------------ | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| source_image_product              | object  | additional info about source image product |
| product_matches                   | array   | result of product verification |
| embedding                      | array   | product embeddings.       |
| box                            | object  | list of parameters of the bounding box for this product         |
| verify  | boolean | failed or success          |
| similarity                     | float   | similarity between this product and the product on the source image               |


### Delete collection

*[Example](examples/product/delete_collection.py)*

To delete an image by ID:

```python
product_collection.delete_collection(collection_name)
```
| Argument  | Type   | Required | Notes                                                        |
| --------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ 
| collection_name    | collection_name  | required | Collection contains sample products.  |

Response:

```
{
    'status': 'completed',
    'result':
    {
        'deleted': <collection_name>
    }
}
```

| Element  | Type   | Description                                                       |
| -------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| status   | string | status of the delete operation.  |
| deleted | string   | name of the removed collection                                          |


## Audit Service

### On Shelf Availability

*[Example](examples/audit/on_shelf_availability.py)*

To check product Availability:

```python
on_shelf_availibility: OnShelfAvailabilityService = deep_vision.init_on_shelf_availability_service(
    RECOGNITION_API_KEY)
on_shelf_availibility.run(collection_name, image_path, list_product_check)
```
| Argument  | Type   | Required | Notes                                                        |
| --------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ 
| collection_name    | collection_name  | required | Collection contains sample products.  |
| image_path         | image   | required | Image can pass from url, local path or bytes. |
| list_product_check         | dict   | required | Dict includes the product name and the quantity needed. |

Response:

```
{
    'status': 'completed', 
    'process_results': {
        'on_shelf_availability': {
            'status': '1', 
            'availability_result': {
                'availability': <ratio>, 
                'unavailability': <ratio>, 
                'not_enough_quantity': <ratio>, 
                'product_availability': [<product_name>], 
                'product_unavailability': [<product_name>], 
                'product_not_enough_quantity': [<product_name>]
            }
        }, 
        'count': {
            <product_name>: int, 
            ...
        }, 
        'verbose': [{
            'base64_image': <base64_iamge>, 
            'locates': [
                {
                    'label': <product_name>, 
                    'score': <score>, 
                    'bbox': <bouding_box>
                },
                ... 
            ]
        }]
    }
}
```

| Element  | Type   | Description                                                       |
| -------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| availability   | float | Proportion of products availability  |
| unavailability   | float | Proportion of products unavailability  |
| not_enough_quantity   | float | Proportion of products not enough quantity   |
| product_availability   | array | list of available products  |
| product_unavailability   | array | list of un available products  |
| product_not_enough_quantity   | array | list of products with insufficient quantity  |

### Adjacencies

*[Example](examples/audit/adjacencies.py)*

To check adjacencies:

```python
adjacencies: AdjacenciesyService = deep_vision.init_audit_adjacencies_service(
    RECOGNITION_API_KEY)
adjacencies.run(collection_name, image_path, adjacent_product)
```
| Argument  | Type   | Required | Notes                                                        |
| --------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ 
| collection_name    | collection_name  | required | Collection contains sample products.  |
| image_path         | image   | required | Image can pass from url, local path or bytes. |
| adjacent_product   | array   | required | array includes products must be adjacent. |

Response:

```
{
    'status': 'completed', 
    'process_results': {
        'adjacencies': 'True/False', 
        'count': {
                <product_name>: int,
            }, 
            'verbose': [{
                'base64_image': <base64_image>, 
                'locates': [
                    {
                        'label': <product_name>, 
                        'score': <score>, 
                        'bbox': <bouding_box>, 
                        'xmin': <x_min>, 
                        'ymin': <y_min>, 
                        'xmax': <x_max>, 
                        'ymax': <y_max>
                    },
                    ... 
                ]
            }]
    }
}

```

| Element  | Type   | Description                                                       |
| -------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| adjacencies   | bool | Are the items next to each other in <adjacent_product>?  |

### Sequence Of Product

*[Example](examples/audit/sequence_of_product.py)*

To check sequence of product:

```python
sequence_of_product: SequenceOfProductService = deep_vision.init_audit_sequence_of_product_service(
    RECOGNITION_API_KEY)
sequence_of_product.run(collection_name, image_path, sequence)
```
| Argument  | Type   | Required | Notes                                                        |
| --------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ 
| collection_name    | collection_name  | required | Collection contains sample products.  |
| image_path         | image   | required | Image can pass from url, local path or bytes. |
| sequence   | array   | required | array specifies the sequence of products. |

Response:

```
{
    'status': 'completed', 
    'process_results': {
        'sequence_of_product': <score>, 
        'count': {
                <product_name>: int,
            }, 
            'verbose': [{
                'base64_image': <base64_image>, 
                'locates': [
                    {
                        'label': <product_name>, 
                        'score': <score>, 
                        'bbox': <bouding_box>, 
                        'xmin': <x_min>, 
                        'ymin': <y_min>, 
                        'xmax': <x_max>, 
                        'ymax': <y_max>
                    },
                ... 
            ]
        }]
    }
}


```

| Element  | Type   | Description                                                       |
| -------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| sequence_of_product   | float | Percentage of products in the correct order  |

